WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
Draw y equals the square root
of x, from nought to four.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.120
Shade the region underneath, then
spin it once round the x-axis.

3
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.540
It sweeps out a solid bowl.

4
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.580
Around it fits a cylinder of
radius two and length four.

5
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.600
Its volume is pi r squared h.

6
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.570
What fraction of that
cylinder does the bowl fill?

7
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.400
A third, like a cone?

8
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.590
More than that?

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.080
In this mission, you'll slice
the solid into thin discs,

10
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.860
each of radius y.

11
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.580
Then you'll add up the
discs with an integral:

12
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.580
V equals the integral
of pi y squared, d x.

13
00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find the volume swept out
when y equals root x spins about the x-axis.
